Translation Scope & Standards
・Full translation of platform UI and both courses into Simplified Chinese.
・Minimum translation scope includes:
・Platform interface (UI elements, navigation, user prompts);
・~45 pages of course content (from Milestone 1: 3 missions × 15 pages/course × 2 courses);
・12 quizzes, 4 submission exercises, 2 peer review tasks;
・Translation reviewed and validated by at least 2 native Chinese-speaking professional translators, each with technical background.
・Translators must meet professional standards: minimum 2 years of translation experience or equivalent certification

ms.promise:
Progress will be measured by the number of founders who complete the program and meet our defined performance metrics, such as code contributions, engagement levels, and NPS scores. Each graduate represents a consistent unit cost, allowing for predictable scaling and efficient resource allocation.
This milestone captures the final delivery, graduation outcomes, and ecosystem contribution of the program. It includes:
・Scaled outreach and founder onboarding beyond the initial 15 participants;
・Graduation of founders who meet defined completion and performance criteria;
・Collection and analysis of program-wide metrics: enrollment, engagement, NPS, and project maturity;
・Publication of a professional-grade final report and closeout video for accountability and knowledge sharing.

ms.criteria:
Program Graduates
・Minimum 40 founders complete the program, defined as:
・Full participation in all 4 curriculum stages;
・Submission of the final project/application aligned with Cardano;
・Completion of feedback surveys;
・Demonstrated activity (e.g., repo commits, integration steps, on-chain interaction).
・Graduation requires achieving:
・≥80% mission completion;
・100% quiz submission rate;
・Final project submission with either a demo, repo, or walkthrough doc.

